  "generated_text": "First, we need to compute $\\mathbf{M}^2$:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M}^2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 11 & -17 \\\\ -26 & 22 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to express $\\mathbf{M}^2$ in the form $p \\mathbf{M} + q \\mathbf{I}$ for some scalars $p$ and $q$.\n\nWe know that:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{M}^2 = \\begin{pmatrix} 11 & -17 \\\\ -26 & 22 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nFrom this, we identify:\n\\[\np = 1, \\quad q = 5.\n\\]\n\nThus, the ordered pair $(p, q)$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{(1, 5)}\n\\]",
